  annotation "note_1771591035072_0", anchor: "since before the Orca Incursion ended", text: "Lianhinglou invokes the Incursion three times and never once attributes intelligence or motive to the orca. They appear only as a natural disaster — weather with teeth and timing. The supply-chain devastation driving every decision in this confession was not random predation. Orca raids are coordinated, theological, purposeful. At least two strikes during the Incursion period were retaliatory, provoked by penguin encroachment on hunting grounds. Acknowledging that would complicate the desperate arithmetic he needs.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771591035072_1", anchor: "What the ice remembers, I forget. Three days, sometimes four. Names slip.", text: "The Walking takes those who have lost much. It is a compulsion rather than a decision — they simply go out onto the ice and do not return. Lianhinglou is losing himself in increments, memory by memory, name by name, but he does not walk out. He walks down. Same erosion, different direction. I wonder whether the Walking and practices like Shell Hatch are not separate phenomena but variations on a single one: the Berg reclaiming what it lent. The harvesters found frozen with peaceful expressions — did they also believe they were doing what the cycle required?", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771591035072_2", anchor: "If you find another way, I will not ask how.", text: "My annotation on the Grand Auditor's entry already identified her crystalline seal on a draft Accord clause authorizing emergency cross-cultural knowledge transfer — frozen in administrative ice, never ratified. She engineered his permission before he departed. He frames it as trust. Both readings are true. I have spent a long career watching people grant each other exactly the latitude they needed to do the thing neither could name aloud, and I recognize the architecture.", type: :correction, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771591035072_3", anchor: "forty-seven days of heating crystal", text: "Forty-seven. Ugly enough to be true. Propaganda rounds up to fifty; panic rounds down to thirty. Requisition officers count to the unit. This is the most trustworthy number in the confession, which is why he made it the title.", type: :pedantic, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771591035072_4", anchor: "The discoloration on my flippers", text: "Geometric spiraling inward is not cold-burn and not Slide Prism residue. The Foundation Depths archive seven documented cases. All involve sustained pressure-depth exposure during blood-sigil work at temperature differentials exceeding twelve degrees. Lianhinglou has read the same archive — his access logs are on file. He is not confused about his own scars. He is performing confusion for an audience he hopes won't check.", type: :correction, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771591035072_5", anchor: "The whisper-echoes in the tunnels are simply pressure acoustics", text: "Whisper-echoes from nothing are a listed corruption marker. Every cleansing assessment filed for that sector confirms active presence. 'Any engineer' would not tell you the same. Any engineer who had worked three fathoms down in the Wane☽ Oncea tunnels and heard those echoes and called them acoustics would be lying for the same reasons Lianhinglou is lying now.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout, source_anchor: "the whisper-echoes in the tunnels are simply pressure acoustics"
  annotation "note_1771591035072_6", anchor: "She never asked me to stop", text: "Seven repetitions. I counted. The entire confession is load-bearing on this phrase — the ethics of a man who built his justification on the silence of someone too hollowed to object. Stratum 7 preserves Mingmeyang's thermal decline across this same period. I documented it. She was freezing from the inside out while he calibrated her arrays with synthesis techniques, and she did not ask him to stop because she could no longer distinguish his help from her deterioration. I have made my own version of this argument — 'no one told me the work should end' — when my committee dissolved and I continued alone. The difference is my work costs only time.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
